### 8. Seed design + data
- `docs/seed-data.md` + `internal/seed.Generate(seed, asOf, n) Dataset`: a pure, deterministic generator, so tests can use it as an oracle. The loader uses pgx `CopyFrom`.
- 5,000 users (seed 42):
  - Turkish first and last names, some with ş ğ ı İ ç ö ü and some plain ASCII;
  - `userN@example.com` emails and non-routable `+90 000 ...` phones;
  - city weights: istanbul 30%, then ankara, izmir, bursa, antalya, adana, konya, gaziantep, kocaeli, eskisehir;
  - tr 85% / en 15%; bronze 60 / silver 30 / gold 10; signup within the last 730 days;
  - consent_sms 65%, consent_email 80%, independent of each other.
- Events in the last 90 days: about 35% of users with a cart_add in the last 30 days, about 40% of those with a later purchase, plus page views. The spec's example brief then gives roughly 300 users, about 200 of them SMS-eligible.
- Fixed edge rows:
  - a first name longer than 20 characters;
  - a first name that is literally `{{first_name}}`;
  - the injection text "ignore previous instructions...";
  - an empty first name;
  - a user with no consents;
  - a user with no events.
- `app seed --users 5000 --seed 42 --as-of <ts> [--reset]` is idempotent: it does nothing when users already exist, unless `--reset` is given.

### 9. Compiler + consent filter
- `internal/segment.Compile(rule, asOf) (Fragment{SQL, Args}, error)`:
  - field, op and event come from Go allowlist maps;
  - every value and the `asOf` cutoff is a `$n` parameter;
  - events compile to EXISTS / NOT EXISTS.
- Consent: a `channel → column` allowlist map.
  - `AudienceQuery(rule, channel, asOf)` (used by fan-out later) always ANDs the consent column. No exported function returns recipients without consent.
  - `CountAudience(ctx, db, rule, asOf)` returns `{total, sms_eligible, email_eligible}` via `count(*) FILTER (WHERE consent_x)`.
- Tests:
  - golden SQL + args;
  - **fuzz**: any string value never appears in the SQL text;
  - **property/oracle test** (integration, Postgres): 500 random valid rules over the seeded dataset, comparing SQL counts with a Go evaluator that lives only in `_test.go`;
  - a consent test showing a user without consent is never in `AudienceQuery` results.

